WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.963
The Patch Bay is the whole instrument, drawn as a hardware faceplate.

2
00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:08.362
Maximize it, and everything is in front of you at once.

3
00:00:08.823 --> 00:00:13.366
Along the top is the Sources bus: every signal you can patch from.

4
00:00:13.366 --> 00:00:16.671
Waveforms, audio, beats, MIDI, and the joystick.

5
00:00:17.123 --> 00:00:18.755
Every parameter gets a cell.

6
00:00:18.755 --> 00:00:23.595
An input jack on the left, a knob with its number, and an output jack on the right.

7
00:00:23.595 --> 00:00:27.618
Turn a knob here, and the same parameter moves in the Controls panel.

8
00:00:28.075 --> 00:00:30.038
Each module has a small i button.

9
00:00:30.038 --> 00:00:35.274
It opens an info panel, with a diagram of everything patched into that module right now.

10
00:00:35.274 --> 00:00:37.595
As you add cables, the diagram follows.

11
00:00:38.049 --> 00:00:42.592
Scroll to zoom the board toward your cursor, and drag empty background to pan.

12
00:00:42.592 --> 00:00:44.922
The hundred percent button puts it back.

13
00:00:46.454 --> 00:00:50.494
Free breaks every module out, so you can arrange the board like a canvas.

14
00:00:50.494 --> 00:00:52.321
Tidy snaps them back into stacks.

15
00:00:52.321 --> 00:00:55.974
Dragging any module by its header does the same for just that one.

16
00:00:56.436 --> 00:00:58.803
Cables run from an output into an input.

17
00:00:58.803 --> 00:01:03.123
Try something that cannot work, and the jack glows red and tells you why.

18
00:01:03.576 --> 00:01:05.294
Next, the cables themselves.
